1. This model represents the core integration layer (DUMEHybridEngine.swift) that orchestrates all the modular components (Compression, Safety, Speculation, Manifold, Storage, Encryption) into a cohesive, production-grade system.
The Intended Engine Model: DUMEHybridEngine

This class is the "brain" of the system. It manages the System Phase (Cold Start → Warming → Active), handles Burst Protection, executes Speculative Reconstruction, and drives Manifold Evolution.
Key Architectural Features

    State Machine: Transitions from coldStart → warming → active based on ingestion count.
    Graceful Degradation: All advanced features (Speculation, Manifold, Burst Protection) are optional and can be disabled at runtime.
    Actor-Based Concurrency: Uses Swift async/await and actors for thread-safe storage and graph updates.
    Deterministic Core: Ensures same input yields same output, critical for reproducibility.

How This Model Works

    Ingest Pipeline:
        Validation: Checks for empty IDs/vectors.
        Phase Check: Determines if the system is in coldStart, warming, or active.
        Burst Detection: If entropy spikes, it disables compression and speculation to ensure 100% fidelity.
        Speculation: If in active mode and not in burst, it predicts the next state based on velocity and confidence.
        Compression: Applies adaptive sparse encoding based on entropy/drift.
        Encryption: Encrypts the compressed data if enabled.
        Storage: Saves the anchor.
        Graph Update: If enabled, adds the node to the k-NN graph and prunes old nodes.

    Retrieval Pipeline:
        Simple lookup in the storage layer. No complex reconstruction logic is needed here because the vector is stored in its final form.

    Lifecycle Management:
        Cold Start (0-100 ingests): No graph, no speculation. Pure deterministic ingestion.
        Warming (100-200 ingests): Graph building begins, speculation is experimental.
        Active (200+ ingests): Full optimization enabled.

Dependencies Required

This engine relies on the following modular components (which should be in their respective folders):

    DUMEMetric (Protocol)
    DUMEPersistentStorage (Protocol + Actors)
    DUMEEncryption (Protocol)
    SparseCompression (Struct)
    SpeculativeEngine (Struct)
    GraphEvolution (Struct)
    BurstDetector (Struct)
    CompressionContext (Struct)
    Anchor (Struct)
    DUMEError (Enum)
    SystemPhase (Enum)

This model ensures that the system is robust, scalable, and production-ready, meeting all the requirements outlined in the repository specification.

